{
  "format": "shaderous-setup",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Double white dwarf fill sweep 3, fill 0.960",
  "blurb": "Two cold carbon-oxygen white dwarfs, 0.6 and 0.9 solar masses, the donor at 0.960 of its Roche lobe (its true radius: the third sweep, after the white dwarf radius fix aaed457, which made every earlier fill 3% low for this donor), settled in the Roche potential and tidally locked, in the frame turning with the orbit. Each threaded by a tangled Kolmogorov field following the square root of the pressure out to the star as it settles (beta about 1e5 throughout, the tip at L1 included); start-up damping over the first 10 time units (rate 1). Helmholtz equation of state; box 16 at 2048^3 with 5 levels. For the onset fill: Mdot against fill after the damping (dwd-sweep.sbatch, dwd-mdot.mjs).",
  "domain": {
    "ndim": 3,
    "n": 2048,
    "amr": 5,
    "box": 16,
    "supports2d": false,
    "bc": {
      "lo": [
        3,
        3,
        3
      ],
      "hi": [
        3,
        3,
        3
      ]
    },
    "units": {
      "name": "white dwarf",
      "length": {
        "unit": "m",
        "value": 10000000
      },
      "mass": {
        "unit": "Msun",
        "value": 1
      }
    }
  },
  "physics": {
